      "title": "Restore leader accuses Farage of ‘outright lying’ over pact offer but says his party ‘remains open’ – UK politics live",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/aug/03/reform-immigration-small-boats-nigel-farage-restore-clacton-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>Rupert Lowe says no talks have taken place after the Reform UK leader said he was ‘open to conversation’ on some sort of electoral deal</p><p>Zia Yusuf said under the plan Reform will create an “integrated surveillance command”, which he claims will “unify” military and intelligence surveillance, making “ours the most surveilled maritime border in the world”.</p><p>“Any vessel attempting to cross illegally will be intercepted by our armed forces who will return them back to France,” he said, adding that emergency legislation would be given to the armed forces to equip them with the “necessary powers”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/aug/03/reform-immigration-small-boats-nigel-farage-restore-clacton-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-03T13:59:57"
    },
    {
      "title": "Farage admits he discussed returning as Reform leader months earlier than previously stated",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/aug/03/nigel-farage-admits-discussed-returning-reform-leader-months-earlier",
      "description": "<p>Admission may undermine Farage’s account of circumstances surrounding £5m gift from crypto billionaire</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/jul/27/andy-burnham-social-care-politics-live-latest-news-defence-nhs-reform-uk-tories-updates\">UK politics live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Nigel Farage has admitted he held talks about the possibility of returning as Reform UK’s leader months before the 2024 general election, potentially undermining his own account of the circumstances in which he received a £5m gift from a crypto billionaire.</p><p>It was <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/aug/02/nigel-farage-deal-political-return-reform-2024-election-reports\">reported at the weekend</a> that Farage had struck a deal with the party’s then leader, Richard Tice, and the convicted fraudster George Cottrell to return to frontline politics.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/aug/03/nigel-farage-admits-discussed-returning-reform-leader-months-earlier\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-03T13:19:20"
    },
    {
      "title": "Standards watchdog investigating Reform UK’s Richard Tice",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/aug/03/standards-watchdog-investigating-reform-richard-tice",
      "description": "<p>Party’s deputy leader says on social media the case is related to a complaint by an anti-Israel lobby group</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/aug/03/reform-immigration-small-boats-nigel-farage-restore-clacton-latest-news-updates\">UK politics live – latest updates</a></p><p>Reform UK’s deputy leader, Richard Tice, is under investigation by parliament’s standards watchdog over a possible failure to declare an interest.</p><p>The watchdog did not provide details of the allegation aside from ⁠saying the case was opened on 28 July and would be conducted by the parliamentary commissioner for standards, Daniel ⁠Greenberg.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/aug/03/standards-watchdog-investigating-reform-richard-tice\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-03T12:25:04"
    },
